    "Strength is measured in MPa (megapascals), a unit of pressure. 1 MPa equals 1 newton of force per square millimetre (about 145 psi). Compressive strength shows how much pressure the concrete can take before it crushes. For example, concrete for houses is usually around 20 to 30 MPa, while high-strength concrete for bridges is 40 MPa or more.\n",
